		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: New GD77/RD5R/DM1801 Beta 2024 10 18]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4500&amp;p=34474#p34474"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><br>Re:DM1801<br><br>Baofeng produced the first version of this for about a year, and its basically a GD77 clone.<br><br>They then re-enginnered the radio and put a different radio in the same case. The new DM1801 is actually just a DMR module, from  mobile phone, plus a PA, rather than descrete ICs.<br><br>AFIK the only way you can identify the difference, without opening the re-engineered radio, is that it doesn't have a direct USB connection.<br>It uses a USB to serial converter dongle in the plug.  I don't have one of these, but I think if you plug the plug into a PC and don't connect the radio, it still appears as a USB device.<br>Whereas the original radio, the USB is handled by the CPU in the radio, and the plug doesn't contain any electronics.<br><br>Because of the confusion of Baofeng releasing the re-enginnered radio, and people finding that they could not install OpenGD77 or OpenRTx on that radio,  Baofeng renamed the radio to be a DR-1801</div></blockquote>Great clarification. Thank you Roger.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5068">KA1CM</a> — Fri Dec 06, 2024 10:38 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
