<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Very nice. Wich zip should I download for the baofeng 1801 for the opengd77 in English?</div></blockquote>OpenDM1801.zip<br><br>Make sure your radio is DM-1801 and supported by openGD77 firmware. DR-1801 is NOT supported, and some of DM-1801 is NOT supported. I don’t have the details on how to tell, maybe waiting for someone who can clarify.</div></blockquote>Re:DM1801<br><br>Baofeng produced the first version of this for about a year, and its basically a GD77 clone.<br><br>They then re-enginnered the radio and put a different radio in the same case. The new DM1801 is actually just a DMR module, from  mobile phone, plus a PA, rather than descrete ICs.<br><br>AFIK the only way you can identify the difference, without opening the re-engineered radio, is that it doesn't have a direct USB connection.<br>It uses a USB to serial converter dongle in the plug.  I don't have one of these, but I think if you plug the plug into a PC and don't connect the radio, it still appears as a USB device.<br>Whereas the original radio, the USB is handled by the CPU in the radio, and the plug doesn't contain any electronics.<br><br>Because of the confusion of Baofeng releasing the re-enginnered radio, and people finding that they could not install OpenGD77 or OpenRTx on that radio,  Baofeng renamed the radio to be a DR-1801<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Dec 06, 2024 10:13 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
